\\times \\frac{3}{4})}^{7}={7}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{7}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02534566-02c5-5597-b335-213a6d95fbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608431} {:answer/id #uuid "07990447-2e77-59ca-9af8-56f9f5420e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{\\pi V}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608437} {:answer/id #uuid "7f293079-44b0-5417-a308-c98657951715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\sqrt[3]{3\\pi V}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608618} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c9d9b7-89e0-5feb-86e5-594989fe32b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{V}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608714} {:answer/id #uuid "f974b91b-f0ea-5c42-b8bc-b7946a5bb42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=27\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02534566-02c5-5597-b335-213a6d95fbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608431} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8c8807b-be58-55b6-bdae-d7e6115dcc88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "505e9ef9-19af-5c96-aca8-bd3dc05a3633" :question/math-academy-id "q-82237" :question/problem "Find an expression for the radius $r$ of the base of a cylinder in terms of its volume $V$ given that the ratio of the radius to the height of the cylinder is $27.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $27,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to express $r$ in terms of $V.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $h$ in the above equation, which we do using cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =27 \\\\ r & =27h \\\\ \\frac{r}{27} & =h \\\\ h & =\\frac{r}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $h=\\frac{r}{27}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ V & =\\pi {r}^{2}(\\frac{r}{27}) \\\\ V & =\\frac{\\pi {r}^{3}}{27}. \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{27V}{\\pi } \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{27V}{\\pi }} \\\\ r & =3\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{\\pi }}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608970 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f1586f-4fd8-57e7-8893-f1ecc0b09a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times \\frac{{4}^{7}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608477} {:answer/id #uuid "7f50bf8d-26bd-50f7-96cb-359544d3d1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{7}\\times {4}^{7}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608619} {:answer/id #uuid "946f384e-aaa8-5b81-a41d-66a19066129b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608651} {:answer/id #uuid "af45221b-41a3-5234-8ff6-1932b4a1242a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times \\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608701} {:answer/id #uuid "d10e09ad-ff01-5c8d-a684-df9e360ecc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{7}\\times {(\\frac{4}{9})}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608763}] :answer