ef 17592186608831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fae5edfd-03b8-5d7c-93f5-427425495794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608831} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa468d18-e1f3-5260-b91b-b03a8928ced4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c6eccb7-973b-5d00-b27a-a6d78b92f54f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72693" :question/problem "In the Atlantic Ocean, a tuna swims $5\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ meters below sea level, while a cormorant flies at $6\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ meters above sea level. If the cormorant is directly above the tuna's position, how far apart are the two animals?" :question/worked-solution "To determine how far apart the two animals are, we must calculate the difference between the locations of the cormorant and the tuna. So, we wish to compute\n\n$$\n6\\,\\frac{1}{2}-(-5\\,\\frac{2}{3}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we convert both mixed numbers to improper fractions. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\cdot 2+1}{2}-(-\\frac{5\\cdot 3+2}{3})\\,\\,\n$$\n\nand simplifying further, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{2}-(-\\frac{17}{3}).\n$$\n\nWe now subtract the two numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{2}-(-\\frac{17}{3}) & =\\frac{13}{2}+\\frac{17}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{6}+\\frac{34}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{39+34}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{6}\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n73÷6=12\\text{R}1=12\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cormorant and the tuna are $12\\frac{1}{6}$ meters apart."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e001840-7e2d-5ca1-9500-4185fa4dc75f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(\\frac{1}